{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Cursed be the man who makes.</b> In Sotah, chapter אלו נאמרין, it is concluded: now is one who serves idolatry not already included in 'cursed'? Rather, this refers to one who lies with a forbidden relative and fathers a son, and the son goes among the nations and serves idolatry. Said the Holy One, blessed be He: cursed be his father and mother, for they caused it. And Rashi explains that there are eleven 'cursed' statements corresponding to the eleven tribes, and corresponding to Simeon no 'cursed' is written, because he was not blessed when Jacob blessed his sons, and it also did not arise in the heart of Moses our teacher to bless him when he blessed the others before his death. And if you ask: what distinguishes these eleven things from all other things? — one may say, because all these are matters between a person and his Maker, and no creature can recognize or know them. And it is found in Shocher Tov: 'taught and taught others, observed and did' — if he had doubt in his hand [i.e., uncertainty] whether to protest and did not protest, lo, he is included in 'cursed be he who does not uphold the words of this Torah.' Did not learn and did not teach, did not observe and did not do — for example, one who was imprisoned in the jailhouse, and had doubt in his hand whether to protest and did protest — lo, he is included in 'blessed be he who upholds the words of this Torah.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:25.749998676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}